{comment: Russian words in Latin letters. Start slowly and speed up through each chorus.}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Kalinka, kalinka, kalinka [E]moya!
V sadu yagoda malinka, malinka [Am]moya!
[Am]Kalinka, kalinka, kalinka [E]moya!
V sadu yagoda malinka, malinka [Am]moya!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Ah, pod [Am]sosnoyu, pod ze[Dm]lenoyu,
Spat' po[E]lozhite vy me[Am]nya!
[Am]Ay-lyuli, lyuli, ay-lyuli, [Dm]lyuli,
Spat' po[E]lozhite vy me[Am]nya!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Ah, [Am]sosenushka ty ze[Dm]lyonaya,
Ne shu[E]mi zhe nado [Am]mnoy!
[Am]Ay-lyuli, lyuli, ay-lyuli, [Dm]lyuli,
Ne shu[E]mi zhe nado [Am]mnoy!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Ah, kra[Am]savitsa, dusha-de[Dm]vitsa,
Po[E]lyubi zhe ty me[Am]nya!
[Am]Ay-lyuli, lyuli, ay-lyuli, [Dm]lyuli,
Po[E]lyubi zhe ty me[Am]nya!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: "Kalinka" is the snowball-tree berry; the verses ask to be laid to sleep under a green pine, and ask a fair maiden for her love.}
{x_end: Am}
